WEBVTT

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:35.010
Alicia sure is late.

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:37.020
I haven't heard from her, either.

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:08.360
"Come here,"

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:18.170
...the wind beckons

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:29.180
"We're face to face,"

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:39.290
...says the sky

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:51.710
A sudden rustle, and you take off...

00:01:51.710 --> 00:02:01.580
...toward the morning sun, as night fades away

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:11.360
With your fingers, you make a rainbow...

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:21.040
...which colors the whole sky

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:31.050
I want to gaze at this world

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:40.320
As it takes my breath away

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:43.510
Huh?

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:47.430
Why am I... not wearing my glove?

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:50.630
Silly Akari.

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:53.220
Ai!

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:58.210
You're a Prima now, so you
don't need your glove anymore.

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:02.030
Eh? I'm a Prima?

00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:04.920
Wait. Ai, when did you?

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:11.800
I'm back, Akari! I was practicing
so hard, I lost track of time!

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:15.010
I'm back, President Aria.

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:17.140
Welcome back!

00:03:17.140 --> 00:03:18.510
Thanks!

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:20.260
Good work today.

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:20.260
That's right...

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:22.120
Dinner's ready.

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:22.610
I'm...

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:24.380
I'm starving!

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:25.120
...a Prima now...

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:25.820
Me too!

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:28.450
That's why...

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:33.710
That's why Alicia won't be
coming here anymore...

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:46.490
A dream?

00:04:09.670 --> 00:04:12.630
Good morning!

00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:14.100
Coming!

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:18.710
Good morning, Woody.

00:04:20.510 --> 00:04:23.980
A refreshing morning calls for fresh eggs!

00:04:23.980 --> 00:04:26.710
Freshly laid eggs, just like you ordered!

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:30.180
Thank you very much.

00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:39.490
The wind feels really nice today, so I'm sure
it'll be another wonderful day, just like yesterday.

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:42.030
Er?

00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:45.500
Oh, yes, it will!

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:49.030
Off I go, then!

00:04:49.030 --> 00:04:50.040
Yes!

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:54.070
Have a nice day!

00:04:54.070 --> 00:04:56.590
Have a nice day!

00:05:15.890 --> 00:05:17.200
My, my.

00:05:28.540 --> 00:05:30.380
What is it, Akari?

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:33.490
Ah, no. It's nothing.

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:42.620
"Dear Ai. Today, morning came to
the Aria Company as it always does...

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:46.860
...and the day started as it always does.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:50.530
It's so familiar, and so wonderful.

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:57.340
But just like my dream last night,
these familiar days will come to an end someday.

00:05:57.340 --> 00:06:02.040
I don't know when that will be,
but in order to face that day with a smile,

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:04.740
I have to practice hard today, too!"

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:04.740
Yay! It's a gondola!

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:06.880
Please wait!

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:08.710
Yippee!

00:06:19.860 --> 00:06:22.260
Oh, no! President Aria!

00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:23.160
Oh, my!

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:24.200
Alicia!

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:25.530
Use this, Akari!

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:26.260
Right!

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:37.910
Thank you, Mr. Cat!

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:40.280
See you later!

00:06:40.630 --> 00:06:42.710
Enjoy the ride!

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:49.460
"Akari, I'm sure an Aria Company
with you in charge...

00:06:49.460 --> 00:06:52.790
...will be an Aria Company filled with wonders.

00:06:52.790 --> 00:06:54.860
Oh, and also!

00:06:54.860 --> 00:06:59.470
It made me kind of happy
that I appeared in your dream."

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:22.750
President Aria...

00:07:24.630 --> 00:07:28.430
Why do you think Alicia chose me?

00:07:40.510 --> 00:07:43.640
I'm sorry for asking such a strange question.

00:07:43.640 --> 00:07:45.480
Ah, the phone.

00:07:47.350 --> 00:07:50.050
Yes, this is the Aria Company.

00:07:50.050 --> 00:07:51.550
Why am I hearing you, Sideburns?

00:07:51.550 --> 00:07:52.780
Ah...

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:56.520
I was calling to hear none other than
Alicia's voice message!

00:07:56.970 --> 00:08:00.490
How dare you interrupt
my sacred moment with Alicia!

00:08:01.130 --> 00:08:03.120
I'm sorry...

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:07.170
Huh? What's wrong?
You seem down this morning.

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:09.250
Ah, it's nothing.

00:08:09.250 --> 00:08:13.840
I'll have to work much harder if I'm
going to replace Alicia someday, won't I?

00:08:14.290 --> 00:08:17.010
That's impossible, Sideburns.

00:08:26.410 --> 00:08:32.990
However, I got to see those fine sideburns
instead, so I'll let this one slide for today.

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:34.330
Be thankful!

00:08:36.060 --> 00:08:38.900
Yes, thank you very much!

00:08:38.900 --> 00:08:39.920
Okay.

00:08:43.530 --> 00:08:46.240
No sappy morning talk allowed.

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:47.670
Huh?

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:51.280
Honestly, Pony-boy needs to stay in character.

00:08:51.280 --> 00:08:53.210
It was out of character, wasn't it?

00:08:53.210 --> 00:08:57.780
But I've had dreams like Akari's, too.

00:08:57.780 --> 00:08:59.380
About your anxieties?

00:08:59.380 --> 00:09:00.420
Yeah.

00:09:00.420 --> 00:09:03.510
I'm so relieved. We're the same, then.

00:09:03.510 --> 00:09:05.620
Don't group me with you!

00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:06.390
Eh?

00:09:06.390 --> 00:09:09.360
In my case, it's not just
about becoming a Prima.

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:13.160
I'll eventually have all of
Himeya to worry about!

00:09:13.660 --> 00:09:16.600
The only thing you'll have to worry about
is President Aria, right?

00:09:17.690 --> 00:09:19.500
I see...

00:09:19.500 --> 00:09:21.540
What about you, Junior?

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:23.940
I expect no problems whatsoever.

00:09:23.940 --> 00:09:25.590
Wow!

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:28.380
What is it?

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:34.320
In your case, when you become a Prima, you might
have to instruct people who are older than you.

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:37.520
That's going to be really awkward, I bet.

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:42.480
But I'm sure Athena wouldn't be
bothered by something like that.

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:49.130
It's just that all three of us have
mentors who are too good.

00:09:49.130 --> 00:09:52.310
They're the Three Great Water Fairies, after all.

00:09:59.030 --> 00:10:00.990
Ah, Al!

00:10:05.170 --> 00:10:06.550
Here you go.

00:10:06.550 --> 00:10:08.950
Thank you very much.

00:10:08.950 --> 00:10:09.950
Sorry to be a bother.

00:10:09.950 --> 00:10:11.790
Don't worry about it.

00:10:15.330 --> 00:10:17.130
Are you shopping, Al?

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:19.230
Yes, for Senryu poetry books.

00:10:19.230 --> 00:10:20.700
Senryu?

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:25.010
Old Man Apa recommended them,
so I've been reading them a lot recently.

00:10:25.010 --> 00:10:30.010
That reminds me. Al, you're an apprentice,
but you're given important tasks, right?

00:10:30.010 --> 00:10:30.810
Yes.

00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:33.510
Is Old Man Apa strict?

00:10:33.510 --> 00:10:38.150
No. Well, I guess it's more that
he's a man of few words.

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:41.990
He prefers the "watch me quietly and learn"
approach when it comes to work.

00:10:41.990 --> 00:10:43.890
Oh?

00:10:43.890 --> 00:10:46.620
There are many different ways
to teach, aren't there?

00:10:47.310 --> 00:10:51.630
I think your mentors match each of you perfectly.

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:56.460
That's true. I'm really glad
that Akira is my mentor.

00:10:56.460 --> 00:10:57.500
I feel the same way!

00:10:57.500 --> 00:10:59.330
Same here.

00:10:59.330 --> 00:11:04.110
I want to live up to Athena's
expectations and repay her someday.

00:11:05.620 --> 00:11:06.510
That's right!

00:11:06.510 --> 00:11:10.010
All we can do for now is work hard,
and try to catch up to them as best we can!

00:11:10.010 --> 00:11:11.070
Right!

00:11:11.820 --> 00:11:12.950
Yeah.

00:11:21.390 --> 00:11:25.460
It's as though Neo-Venezia
and the birds are cheering us on.

00:11:25.460 --> 00:11:26.960
No sappy lines allowed!

00:11:26.960 --> 00:11:28.200
Huh?!

00:11:42.850 --> 00:11:44.480
Welcome back!

00:11:44.480 --> 00:11:46.750
I had so much fun. It was fantastic!

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:49.490
I'm an Alicia fan now!

00:11:49.490 --> 00:11:50.670
Yes!

00:11:52.380 --> 00:11:53.790
Me too, me too!

00:11:53.790 --> 00:11:56.360
My, my. Thank you very much.

00:11:58.260 --> 00:12:00.970
The President is cute, too!

00:12:00.970 --> 00:12:02.410
It's nice and cold!

00:12:02.830 --> 00:12:04.600
Ah! Me too, me too!

00:12:04.900 --> 00:12:06.270
It feels so nice.

00:12:06.270 --> 00:12:08.810
Oh, it does feel nice.

00:12:08.810 --> 00:12:10.340
Good work.

00:12:10.340 --> 00:12:11.810
And to you, too.

00:12:11.810 --> 00:12:14.480
Um, President...

00:12:14.480 --> 00:12:17.360
May I touch your tummy as an added bonus?

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:19.780
It's so pudgy-wudgy!

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:22.750
Ah! Me too, me too!

00:12:22.750 --> 00:12:23.820
Wow...

00:12:23.820 --> 00:12:25.280
My, my...

00:12:24.420 --> 00:12:25.760
It's so pudgy-wudgy!

00:12:47.510 --> 00:12:51.880
Akari, let's have some tea
after you finish cleaning up.

00:12:51.880 --> 00:12:52.920
Okay!

00:12:54.260 --> 00:12:58.120
I made bracken dumplings, so could you
get them out of the fridge please?

00:12:58.120 --> 00:12:59.190
Sure!

00:13:01.230 --> 00:13:02.450
My, my.

00:13:05.510 --> 00:13:07.670
Here you go, President Aria.

00:13:18.490 --> 00:13:20.760
Delicious!

00:13:39.870 --> 00:13:42.030
Um, Alicia...

00:13:44.200 --> 00:13:48.110
Last night, I dreamt I was a Prima.

00:13:48.110 --> 00:13:50.430
My, my, how wonderful.

00:13:51.340 --> 00:13:52.610
But...

00:13:52.610 --> 00:13:55.950
...you were no longer there.

00:13:58.460 --> 00:14:04.190
There was even a new Pair,
but I wasn't confident at all in my dream.

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:11.970
It made me realize that I have a
long way to go until I can be like you.

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:16.830
That's why I'm going to
work much, much harder!

00:14:19.350 --> 00:14:22.440
When I became a Prima...

00:14:23.990 --> 00:14:30.010
...and the time came for Grandma,
who had always been here with me, to leave...

00:14:30.010 --> 00:14:33.180
...I said something selfish.

00:14:38.290 --> 00:14:40.760
I wasn't sure if I'd be able to
manage on my own.

00:14:40.760 --> 00:14:45.400
So, for the first time, I said
something selfish to Grandma.

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:47.930
Please, Grandma!

00:14:47.930 --> 00:14:49.300
Please stay!

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:56.240
No! I can't bear it!

00:14:56.240 --> 00:14:59.210
Please don't leave me by myself!

00:15:00.250 --> 00:15:05.180
Parting ways is lonely, but it's not
something you should be sad about.

00:15:07.170 --> 00:15:08.120
Besides...

00:15:08.990 --> 00:15:12.620
...I'm not leaving you.

00:15:12.620 --> 00:15:16.130
You're leaving me, to set out on your own.

00:15:17.090 --> 00:15:21.110
You'll be just fine. After all, you're a Prima now!

00:15:27.110 --> 00:15:32.150
Her back had always
given me a sense of security.

00:15:37.910 --> 00:15:44.460
Even after Akira and Athena became
Primas and took on apprentices...

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:50.370
...I still didn't think I'd ever be able to teach
someone as well as Grandma had taught me.

00:15:58.830 --> 00:16:01.030
Hey, Alicia!

00:16:02.420 --> 00:16:05.940
Akira, Aika! Hello.

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:08.450
Alicia! Hello!

00:16:08.450 --> 00:16:10.650
You're looking worn out as usual.

00:16:11.010 --> 00:16:12.620
My, my.

00:16:12.970 --> 00:16:15.750
It's because you're still
doing everything by yourself!

00:16:15.750 --> 00:16:19.560
Well? Have you considered
taking on an apprentice yet?

00:16:19.560 --> 00:16:20.890
All right!

00:16:20.890 --> 00:16:23.790
Are you finally going to
have an apprentice, Alicia?!

00:16:23.790 --> 00:16:24.360
Hey!

00:16:24.400 --> 00:16:25.760
Wha?

00:16:26.210 --> 00:16:29.170
You're the heir to Himeya.

00:16:29.170 --> 00:16:31.970
Yes, I know...

00:16:33.500 --> 00:16:38.140
I wonder what kind of girl
Alicia will teach? I'm so jealous!

00:16:38.140 --> 00:16:39.470
My, my.

00:16:40.930 --> 00:16:43.980
Hey, Alicia. Are you free tomorrow evening?

00:16:45.450 --> 00:16:46.250
Yes.

00:16:46.250 --> 00:16:49.090
Good. Don't take any jobs, keep it open.

00:16:49.900 --> 00:16:51.360
You're coming with me.

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:52.120
Wha?!

00:16:52.580 --> 00:16:54.990
What's going on? A duel?!

00:17:00.530 --> 00:17:03.000
Just you wait! Your head is mine!

00:17:05.940 --> 00:17:07.330
My, my.

00:17:11.380 --> 00:17:13.680
Where are we going, Akira?

00:17:13.680 --> 00:17:15.850
Relax, you'll find out soon enough.

00:17:42.140 --> 00:17:44.110
The Campanile?

00:17:44.110 --> 00:17:46.180
We haven't climbed it in a long time, right?

00:17:46.180 --> 00:17:47.210
Yeah.

00:17:48.250 --> 00:17:50.890
It's good to climb it every once in a while.

00:18:08.830 --> 00:18:10.100
Athena!

00:18:10.100 --> 00:18:13.600
Ah, Alicia. Welcome!

00:18:13.600 --> 00:18:15.110
I've been waiting for you.

00:18:15.110 --> 00:18:16.210
For me?

00:18:16.210 --> 00:18:21.480
Yep. Akira said the three of us should
go up the Campanile together.

00:18:21.480 --> 00:18:23.580
I haven't been up here in ages!

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:27.840
Look, Alicia! You can see the entire city!

00:18:30.790 --> 00:18:35.280
This is the city we live in...

00:18:36.830 --> 00:18:41.370
This view makes you fall in love with
the city all over again, doesn't it?

00:18:41.370 --> 00:18:42.930
It does.

00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:49.510
Delivering the wonders of this city to our
customers' hearts is our job, isn't it?

00:18:50.370 --> 00:18:55.480
The original Campanile back on Manhome
collapsed several times, apparently.

00:18:56.150 --> 00:19:02.420
But despite that, the people
of Venice rebuilt it every time.

00:19:02.420 --> 00:19:04.050
Oh?

00:19:04.780 --> 00:19:10.030
I'm sure the people of Venice wanted to
pass on this view to the next generation.

00:19:11.930 --> 00:19:13.960
It's like Undines.

00:19:14.950 --> 00:19:19.050
Just like our mentors who taught us,

00:19:19.050 --> 00:19:22.270
we'll have to walk away
from our gondolas someday, too.

00:19:22.270 --> 00:19:28.350
But if we're able to pass on
our love for this city...

00:19:28.350 --> 00:19:32.950
...the next generation of Undines
will become the new Campanile.

00:19:34.670 --> 00:19:38.350
The new... Campanile...

00:19:52.770 --> 00:19:56.530
Doesn't this song make you
happy when you hear it?

00:20:27.350 --> 00:20:31.110
We're a brand new Campanile.

00:20:31.990 --> 00:20:34.310
We can't do everything perfectly from the start.

00:20:35.650 --> 00:20:37.600
You shouldn't be so hard on yourself.

00:20:38.650 --> 00:20:39.710
Yeah.

00:20:43.120 --> 00:20:44.490
Thank you...

00:20:45.650 --> 00:20:49.530
...Akira, Athena.

00:20:52.510 --> 00:20:55.970
That's when I finally understood.

00:20:56.580 --> 00:20:58.540
Even though I was full of uncertainty,

00:20:58.540 --> 00:21:02.870
I wanted to pass down the wonders
that Grandma had shown me...

00:21:02.870 --> 00:21:05.980
...along with the ones I discovered myself.

00:21:34.300 --> 00:21:35.680
And then...

00:21:47.750 --> 00:21:49.090
Huh?

00:21:49.090 --> 00:21:51.590
My, my. You're awake...

00:21:51.590 --> 00:21:53.510
...Miss Akari Mizunashi.

00:21:55.050 --> 00:21:56.280
Yes?

00:21:59.910 --> 00:22:03.410
Welcome to Aria Company.

00:22:06.390 --> 00:22:10.110
Then, you came along, Akari.

00:22:19.890 --> 00:22:20.820
Um...

00:22:20.820 --> 00:22:22.220
What is it?

00:22:22.220 --> 00:22:25.480
Well... Um...

00:22:26.250 --> 00:22:29.190
Why did you choose me?

00:22:35.830 --> 00:22:37.170
That's a secret.

00:22:37.170 --> 00:22:38.840
Huh?

00:22:42.060 --> 00:22:46.080
Then, weren't you worried,
with me as your new assistant?

00:22:46.080 --> 00:22:49.010
My, my. Why?

00:22:49.010 --> 00:22:52.980
Well, I was asleep when I arrived...

00:22:52.980 --> 00:22:54.420
...and I sculled backwards...

00:22:56.790 --> 00:22:58.760
Say, Akari.

00:22:59.810 --> 00:23:02.830
Why don't we go up the Campanile together?

00:23:02.830 --> 00:23:05.100
Eh? Ah... Sure.

00:23:05.100 --> 00:23:10.680
But we're fully booked this week,
so we can't take any time off.

00:23:14.220 --> 00:23:15.710
How about right now?

00:23:15.710 --> 00:23:17.170
Huh?!

00:23:18.280 --> 00:23:22.250
Right now? Will they even let us in at this hour?

00:23:22.250 --> 00:23:23.770
Let's find out!

00:24:36.460 --> 00:24:38.890
It's closed after all...

00:24:38.890 --> 00:24:41.160
Over here, Akari.

00:24:41.160 --> 00:24:42.130
Huh?

00:24:45.600 --> 00:24:47.900
Ah, please wait!

00:24:49.900 --> 00:24:50.800
Ah!

00:24:50.800 --> 00:24:52.670
My, my.

00:24:52.670 --> 00:24:56.370
This gentleman is from the
Campanile's management association.

00:24:56.900 --> 00:24:59.750
I contacted him before we left.

00:25:00.530 --> 00:25:03.250
I've been waiting for you. Here, come in.

00:25:04.230 --> 00:25:07.220
This entrance is usually off limits,

00:25:07.220 --> 00:25:10.290
but I'll make an exception
since it's for you, Alicia.

00:25:10.290 --> 00:25:11.920
Thank you very much.

00:25:22.500 --> 00:25:24.070
Wow!

00:25:24.070 --> 00:25:27.480
So this is what it looks like inside!

00:25:52.060 --> 00:25:55.700
It's a mysterious sound, isn't it?

00:25:55.700 --> 00:25:57.610
A mysterious sound?

00:25:58.140 --> 00:25:59.230
Yes.

00:26:01.500 --> 00:26:06.010
It's quiet, deep, and gentle...

00:26:06.770 --> 00:26:09.980
This sound has been echoing
through these corridors...

00:26:09.980 --> 00:26:13.120
...ever since the Campanile was born, hasn't it?

00:26:15.890 --> 00:26:18.290
Wow, that's amazing!

00:26:18.710 --> 00:26:21.590
You can see Piazza San Marco from here!

00:26:21.590 --> 00:26:22.960
My, my.

00:26:25.740 --> 00:26:26.900
I see...

00:26:28.770 --> 00:26:31.700
This city is alive!

00:26:31.700 --> 00:26:35.640
So this sound must be its breath.

00:26:38.340 --> 00:26:40.380
Yes, I think so, too.

00:26:47.950 --> 00:26:49.190
Akari.

00:26:49.190 --> 00:26:50.320
Yes?

00:26:53.310 --> 00:27:03.850
Such a gentle feeling, like the breeze

00:27:02.700 --> 00:27:04.370
Come on, let's go.

00:27:04.820 --> 00:27:14.190
I want to protect it, tenderly

00:27:07.040 --> 00:27:08.350
Okay...

00:27:16.230 --> 00:27:26.630
You've taught me something so important

00:27:26.660 --> 00:27:31.630
When I chose you as my apprentice,
the only thing I was worried about...

00:27:27.640 --> 00:27:37.540
This city by the water is so dear to me

00:27:31.630 --> 00:27:37.100
...was whether or not I would
be a good mentor for you.

00:27:37.650 --> 00:27:49.460
I'm surrounded by a gentle, bittersweet warmth

00:27:39.180 --> 00:27:45.170
But you always stood by me, without any hesitation.

00:27:46.340 --> 00:27:53.360
With your pure heart, you discovered many wonders that I hadn't noticed.

00:27:49.460 --> 00:27:59.370
Looking straight ahead, I start to walk

00:27:56.720 --> 00:28:00.960
You gave me my confidence, Akari.

00:28:01.210 --> 00:28:09.510
I'll walk tomorrow too, until the sun sets

00:28:10.380 --> 00:28:20.780
I will weave these humble feelings

00:28:15.510 --> 00:28:19.370
I feel a bit ticklish inside.

00:28:24.480 --> 00:28:26.480
Okay, we're here.

00:28:26.480 --> 00:28:30.070
Ah, so this is where it leads!

00:28:31.350 --> 00:28:32.960
Wow!

00:28:35.930 --> 00:28:39.760
Amazing, amazing! This is amazing!

00:28:40.450 --> 00:28:51.860
As the seasons and colors change,

00:28:51.860 --> 00:28:57.960
I want to feel them, as if they were in my hands

00:28:57.960 --> 00:29:05.900
Right now, at this very moment

00:29:00.580 --> 00:29:04.400
The Aria Company is in this direction, right?

00:29:06.910 --> 00:29:15.370
Tomorrow too, until the sun sets

00:29:16.120 --> 00:29:27.560
I want to weave these humble feelings for you

00:29:19.840 --> 00:29:24.040
Someday, the time will come for us to go our separate ways.

00:29:24.040 --> 00:29:28.980
But for now, would it be all right
if I stayed close to this person,

00:29:28.980 --> 00:29:33.850
whom I love and cherish dearly,
for just a little while longer?

00:29:29.730 --> 00:29:40.410
That warm smile that was given to me...

00:29:40.410 --> 00:29:55.580
...will continue to guide my happiness,

00:29:58.320 --> 00:30:03.460
As I head on toward the sunset
